 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to refunding penalties accrued on certain real property\ntaxes in the town of Scarsdale, county of Westchester",
    "basePrintNo": "S9202",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9202-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9202\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to refunding penalties accrued on certain real prop-\nerty taxes in the town of Scarsdale, county of Westchester\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo allow the town of Scarsdale to refund penalties to certain real prop-\nerty taxpayers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows the Custodian of Taxes of the town of Scarsdale, upon\napproval by the Scarsdale Town Board, to refund any penalties accrued on\nreal property taxes where the property owner failed to pay their school\ntaxes on or before September 30, 2023, or on or before September 30,\n2023 and January 31, 2024 if electing to pay in two installments, as a\nresult of the United States Postal Service's failure to deliver the real\nproperty tax bill to the property owner.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn August and September 2023, several Scarsdale residents did not\nreceive their real property tax bills due to a failure by the United\nStates Postal Service to deliver the bills. Due to this, several real\nproperty owners in the town paid their school taxes after the due date\nand incurred penalties. This legislation would allow the Scarsdale\nCustodian of Taxes, upon approval of the Town Board, to refund any\npenalties accrued by residents who did not pay their school taxes before\nthe due date because such tax bills were not delivered by USPS.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
